      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems wrong, that there is a #warning and then an #error.\n\nI think this file logic perhaps should be:\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_FPU) || defined(CONFIG_SOFT_FLOAT) /* and maybe !NEWLIB_LIBC) */\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M\n...\n#elif CONFIG_RISCV\n\nThe #warning is here if SOFT_FLOAT enabled, and I think this means\nthat the extra functions are already handled, but not sure about what should happen with non SOFT_FLOAT. Why is there a warning here?\nMaybe separate this from the non-RISCV error:\n\n#ifndef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_SOFT_FLOAT\n#error \"RISCV HW FPU not supported\"\n#endif\n\n#else\n#error \"Unsupported core: please add an implementation\"\n#endif",
      "revId": "3bbd78cb13cfa12f4af607b000a4f9463a08e742",
